.Dd February 6, 2026
.Dt VFS_FHTOVP 9
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm vfs_fhtovp
.Nd turn an NFS file handle into a vnode
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/param.h
.In sys/mount.h
.In sys/vnode.h
.Ft int
.Fn vfs_fhtovp "struct mount *mp" "struct fid *fhp" "struct vnode **vpp"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Fn vfs_fhtovp
function converts a file handle
.Fa fhp
into a vnode for the filesystem
.Fa mp .
The vnode is returned in
.Fa *vpp
with a reference count incremented.
.Pp
Arguments:
.Bl -tag -width ".Fa vpp"
.It Fa mp
The mounted filesystem.
.It Fa fhp
Pointer to the file handle.
.It Fa vpp
Pointer to a vnode pointer where the result will be stored.
.El
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Returns 0 on success, or an error code on failure.
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width ".Bq Er EOPNOTSUPP"
.It Bq Er EOPNOTSUPP
The filesystem does not support this operation.
.It Bq Er ESTALE
The file handle is stale (file deleted or filesystem changed).
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr vfs_mount 9 ,
.Xr vfs_vget 9
